WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.340
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:14.026
Our show has a voice, a job and a rival, but it's got nowhere to go!

5
00:00:14.026 --> 00:00:16.783
Today we build the map: realms, regions,

6
00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:20.917
locations and areas, and how they all fit inside each other.

7
00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:24.874
Think of it like boxes in boxes.

8
00:00:24.874 --> 00:00:27.177
The realm is the whole world.

9
00:00:27.177 --> 00:00:29.956
Regions are the squares on the map.

10
00:00:29.956 --> 00:00:33.926
Locations are places inside a region, like a town.

11
00:00:33.926 --> 00:00:39.008
And areas are the spots inside a location, like the high street.

12
00:00:39.008 --> 00:00:41.549
Most worlds only need one realm.

13
00:00:42.933 --> 00:00:46.385
Open Map, then Realms, and there's ours, The Trade Roads.

14
00:00:46.385 --> 00:00:50.019
A realm is the top box, the whole world your story lives in,

15
00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:54.984
and you only need a second one for something like a dream world or a shadow world.

16
00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:58.821
Basic info is what the narrator reads about it.

17
00:00:58.821 --> 00:01:02.713
Mine says every town on these roads makes its own law.

18
00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:06.476
Initial known means players can see it from the start.

19
00:01:06.476 --> 00:01:10.214
Players can only reach places inside a realm they know about.

20
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.405
Next, Map, then Regions.

21
00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:18.141
We've got two: The Hollow Counties, all farms and market towns,

22
00:01:18.141 --> 00:01:22.653
and The Gloamwood, the old forest where the bad stuff lives.

23
00:01:22.653 --> 00:01:24.232
Here's the first one.

24
00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:28.069
Basic info again, what the narrator reads.

25
00:01:28.069 --> 00:01:31.633
Farms, hedges, a church spire in every town.

26
00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:35.201
Realm says which world it belongs to.

27
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.753
And X and Y are its square on the map grid.

28
00:01:38.753 --> 00:01:40.618
X goes east, Y goes north.

29
00:01:40.618 --> 00:01:46.288
Next door means one apart, so the Gloamwood sits at one, zero, right beside us.

30
00:01:46.288 --> 00:01:47.938
Keep the numbers small.

31
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:52.747
Up top, the Map tab shows it all laid out.

32
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.999
There's the Hollow Counties with Mudbury as a dot, and the Gloamwood right next door.

33
00:01:57.999 --> 00:02:04.096
You see every square in Studio, but players see a region they haven't found yet as fog with a question mark,

34
00:02:04.096 --> 00:02:05.959
until the story takes them there.

35
00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:11.789
Now Map, then Locations, and our first town, Mudbury.

36
00:02:11.789 --> 00:02:17.128
A location is a place inside a region: a town, a castle, a cave.

37
00:02:17.128 --> 00:02:19.464
Players travel to locations.

38
00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:22.396
Basic info is what everyone can see.

39
00:02:22.396 --> 00:02:27.458
Five hundred stubborn souls, mud to the ankle, and a mayor who hates fun.

40
00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.203
Complexity type.

41
00:02:29.203 --> 00:02:32.950
Simple is one spot, like a tavern or a shrine.

42
00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:38.732
Complex has areas inside it, joined by paths, like a town or a dungeon.

43
00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:44.254
Size is how big it is on the map, and how far out it catches travellers.

44
00:02:44.254 --> 00:02:47.363
If two places overlap, the smaller one wins.

45
00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.936
Hidden info is the secret only the narrator knows.

46
00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:53.947
The best ones are something happening right now.

47
00:02:53.947 --> 00:02:58.713
Mine? The mayor's taking Gilt Circus money, and he let the lion out himself.

48
00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:04.447
Detail type. Basic lets Voyage write the areas and secrets for you.

49
00:03:04.447 --> 00:03:07.363
Detailed uses exactly what you wrote.

50
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.805
And down the bottom, its areas, the spots inside the town.

51
00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.069
The rest of the form, quickly.

52
00:03:15.069 --> 00:03:20.489
Initial known puts it on the map from the start, otherwise players find it by visiting.

53
00:03:20.489 --> 00:03:23.915
Hidden takes it off the map until a trigger reveals it.

54
00:03:23.915 --> 00:03:27.092
Visual tags are a few words that guide its picture.

55
00:03:27.092 --> 00:03:31.764
And factions and N P C level range say who's around and how tough they are.

56
00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:34.839
Last one, Map, then Areas.

57
00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:38.506
Every area belongs to a location, and here are Mudbury's.

58
00:03:38.506 --> 00:03:43.523
Here's a thing that trips people up: the first area on the list is the way in.

59
00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:48.991
Arrive without picking an area and that's where you land, so put your entrance first.

60
00:03:48.991 --> 00:03:50.535
Ours is the high street.

61
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.588
The description is what the space is like,

62
00:03:53.588 --> 00:03:57.223
what people do there, and one detail you can smell or hear.

63
00:03:57.667 --> 00:04:00.811
And paths are the other areas you can walk to from here.

64
00:04:00.811 --> 00:04:05.303
The high street joins up to the butcher's yard, the mayor's garden and our camp,

65
00:04:05.303 --> 00:04:09.346
and each of those lists the high street back, so you can walk both ways.

66
00:04:10.733 --> 00:04:13.221
Studio has its own checklist for this.

67
00:04:13.221 --> 00:04:17.739
A place is playable once it has a background, a region and its areas.

68
00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:22.452
It's polished once it has a picture, visual tags, factions and a secret.

69
00:04:22.452 --> 00:04:26.774
Get it playable first, and put the way in at the top of the areas.

70
00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.052
And that's the whole map, boxes in boxes.

71
00:04:31.052 --> 00:04:34.853
Everything from this one is linked in the description.

72
00:04:34.853 --> 00:04:39.498
Next time, the rest of the map folder, and the slow bit, pictures.

73
00:04:39.933 --> 00:04:43.881
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

